I commented on and closed one issue, #1010, and left the rest alone.

#1010 (fixed and closed): Task 1 (commit 8988d853) fixes it.
• **Segment check:** when you have a deny list, each part of a compound command is now checked on its own, with leading `VAR=value` and `export`-style prefixes removed. So cd x && rm -rf build and TZ=UTC rm -rf build both hit rm -rf *.
• **Indirect commands:** a command whose program name comes from `$X`, `$(...)` or backticks is refused. That covers `X=rm; $X -rf ~` and the other two bypasses from the issue's table.
• **Trade-off:** with a deny list, `"$CARGO" build` is now refused too, and a test pins that. With no deny list nothing changes, so the evolve loop isn't affected. Tests also pin the bypasses and the no-list case.
• **Still open:** a command built at runtime and run via eval "$(...)" still gets past the check. It's filed as #1011 and the permissions docs now state the limit.

